---
import "../styles/globals.css";
import SEO from "../components/SEO.astro";

const siteUrl = "https://zentype.jonathanrreed.com";
const aboutUrl = `${siteUrl}/about/`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<SEO
			title="Zen Typer Background and Private Typing Practice"
			description="Who built Zen Typer, why the typing practice app exists, and how it keeps mindful typing account-free with everything stored in your browser."
			canonical={aboutUrl}
			keywords={[
				"Zen Typer about",
				"mindful typing app",
				"typing practice app",
				"Jonathan R. Reed typing app",
			]}
			breadcrumbItems={[
				{ name: "Mindful typing test", url: `${siteUrl}/` },
				{ name: "About Zen Typer", url: aboutUrl },
			]}
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main class="content-page px-6 pb-32 pt-16 text-text">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8">
				<nav aria-label="Primary" class="content-nav">
					<a href="/">Home</a>
					<a href="/quote/">Quote mode</a>
					<a href="/zen/">Zen mode</a>
					<a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
					<a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
					<a href="/subprocessors/">Subprocessors</a>
				</nav>

				<article class="glass content-prose rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 space-y-8 stagger-fade-in">
					<header class="space-y-4 border-b border-iris/15 pb-7">
						<p class="eyebrow text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.28em]">About</p>
						<h1>About Zen Typer</h1>
						<p class="!text-lg !leading-8">
							Zen Typer is a typing app built by Jonathan R. Reed. It measures speed and accuracy without turning the session into a race.
						</p>
					</header>

					<section class="space-y-4">
						<h2>Why it exists</h2>
						<p>
							Most typing sites are built around leaderboards and a timer counting down at you. I wanted the useful parts without the rest: a good passage to type, a mark on every character, a number at the end, and a record of whether I'm getting better. Most days it's a warmup before real work. Some days it's the accuracy drill I owe myself, and now and then it's just somewhere to get words moving when the blank page is the problem.
						</p>
						<p>
							Quote Mode is the measured half. A short passage from a public-domain book, a mark on every character as you type it, and WPM and accuracy at the end. There are 322 quotes from 22 writers, and each one names its source. Zen Mode is the open half. Words drift up the canvas as you finish them, everything is saved as a draft, and the stats sit in the corner instead of in the way.
						</p>
						<p>
							Sound is there if you want it and off if you don't. The keyboard switches and the rain are synthesized in the browser, so nothing is downloaded and nothing plays until you turn it on.
						</p>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-4">
						<h2>Privacy and design principles</h2>
						<p>
							There's no account and no server that sees what you type. Settings, drafts, and session history are written to your browser and stay there. If you want them somewhere else, one button exports everything to a file and another restores it. The whole app works from the keyboard, and it drops the animation it doesn't need when your system asks for reduced motion.
						</p>
						<p>
							The project stays small on purpose. The source is on GitHub under the MIT license, and the <a href="/whats-new/">what's new page</a> says what changed in each release.
						</p>
					</section>
				</article>
			</div>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
